now to ukraine where russia has  intensified its attacks on the eastern  and southern parts of that country and  the ukrainians they are fighting back  this video from the russian military  claims to show damage in russian  occupied territory charlie dagetta went  to the ukrainian front lines and spoke  to some of those who are fighting  including an american veteran  explosions rocked the southern city of  kirsan overnight  residents have been protesting the  russian occupation  and ukraine has made clear it has no  intention of giving it up  still trapped beneath the steel plant in  mariopol a ukrainian officer pleads for  an evacuation of hundreds  the war has become a brutal artillery  battle waged along a jagged front in  southern and eastern ukraine where we  visited the front lines  as you can see this is a freshly dug  trench and it's a fallback position for  ukrainian soldiers who've been defending  the russian advance not far from here  the commander told us the fighting has  been so intense the russians launched  1500 mortars on a single position in a  single day  special forces battalion commander igor  lapin said they simply do not have the  firepower to match russia  the biggest difficulty is that we're  running short on high caliber ammunition  he said the military is always hungry  for ammo  and hungry for experienced warriors like  iraq war marine veteran and alaska  native joshua cropper you're willing to  put your life on the line for another  country  yes sir what is it like fighting beside  these ukrainian forces i wish that they  had a more nato experience more nato  training  but uh more nato weapons more nato  weapons but their their hearts in the  right place and their convictions in the  right place  former royal air force serviceman jordan  davis left a five-year-old daughter back  home in the uk uh you realize you're  about as close as you can get to the  front line are you prepared for what may  happen absolutely you're willing to die  i am willing to die here if needs be  that position was within easy reach of  russian artillery and russian forces are  closing in on three sides the ukrainian  commander told us they haven't received  any of america's heavy weapons at that  location yet  tony all right charlie daggett in  ukraine for us once again charlie thank  you very much
 

